# Foundry build artifacts - fully reproducible from src/ + lib/, not
# committed.
out/
cache/
cache_forge/
broadcast/

# lib/ (forge-std, openzeppelin-contracts) is DELIBERATELY vendored/
# committed here, NOT gitignored - see README.md's "Dependencies" section
# for why (fresh-clone reproducibility without depending on network access
# to GitHub at build/CI time). Re-running `forge install` would also work
# and produce the same pinned versions (forge-std 1.16.2,
# openzeppelin-contracts 5.7.0 - see README.md), but isn't required.

# test-vectors.json IS committed (deliberately not ignored) - it's the
# deliverable the downstream TS-parity task consumes, regenerated by
# `forge test` (see test/GenerateTestVectors.t.sol).
